      "type": "grammar",
      "title": "了 for a change: \"now it's…\"",
      "body": "Put 了 at the end of a sentence to show that something has changed and is now true. 下雨 means \"to rain\", but 下雨了 means \"it's started raining\" or \"it's raining now\". With 不, it means \"not anymore\".",
